OL,3,GNEWSASeal 'anchored' down by debris
OL,4,Aneeds months of care
OL,5,
OL,6,FA seal that became tangled in a heavy
OL,7,F"anchor" of fishing nets, ropes and
OL,8,Fhooks is in a "touch and go" condition,
OL,9,Fthe RSPCA has said.
OL,11,FThe year-old seal, named Doughnut by
OL,12,Fcarers, had her neck sliced open by a
OL,13,F4kg (8.8lbs) twisted mass of ropes and
OL,14,Fdebris and is now receiving emergency
OL,15,Ftreatment at the RSPCA's East Winch
OL,16,Fwildlife centre in Norfolk.
OL,18,FShe was rescued from Horsey on Sunday
OL,19,Fwhen volunteers from Friends of Horsey
OL,20,FSeals hauled her out of the sea after
OL,21,Ftheir concerns deepened over weeks of
OL,22,Fspotting her trapped.
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
